IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g2-nouns`
IMPORT `g2-readings`
IMPORT `g2-art5-charity-test`
IMPORT `g2-art6-purposes`
IMPORT `g2-art7-public-benefit`

IMPORT `ind-b-tests-fixtures-g2`

-- ind-b-tests-art5-7: independent tests of Articles 5 to 7 (group G2), by test author ind-b.
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the Law before this module's imports were opened; each assertion cites its row id.
-- An assertion of this file is expected to pass; one that fails was moved to ind-b-tests-disagree.l4 or ind-b-tests-ambiguous.l4, never edited.

§ `Article 5 -- the charity test (rows E5-01 to E5-29)`

-- E5-01: sole purpose education, public benefit to a reasonable degree: meets.
#ASSERT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-02: relief of poverty and a purely ancillary shop: meets.
#ASSERT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b poverty`, `ind-b shop`) `ind-b none` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-03: education and profit for members: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`, `ind-b profit`) `ind-b none` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-04: only an ancillary purpose, no charitable one: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b shop`) `ind-b none` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-05: charitable purposes, public benefit not to a reasonable degree: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b no PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-06: an applicant that intends to provide public benefit: meets.
#ASSERT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b applicant` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b intended PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-07: a registered charity that only intends to provide public benefit: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b intended PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-07 (restricted section): the same.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `entered in the restricted section` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b intended PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-08: public benefit elsewhere than Jersey: meets (the encoding carries no place; the finding is "in Jersey or elsewhere").
#ASSERT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-09: an applicant that neither provides nor intends to provide: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b applicant` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b no PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-10: constitution lets a Minister, acting as such, direct the activities: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-11: constitution lets a governor be a member of the States Assembly, acting as such: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-12: constitution lets the equivalent of a Minister elsewhere, acting as such, control the activities: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` `any equivalent of a Minister or of a member of the States Assembly in another jurisdiction` TRUE) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-13: a States member may be a governor in a personal capacity only: meets.
#ASSERT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` FALSE) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-14: constitution silent: meets.
#ASSERT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-15: as E5-10, and an Order under 5(3) disapplies 5(2): meets.
#ASSERT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` TRUE
-- E5-15: the entity then meets the test only by virtue of the Order.
#ASSERT `Art 5(3) the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE) `the Chief Minister` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` TRUE
-- E5-16: fails 5(1), has a 5(2) provision, an Order disapplies 5(2): does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`, `ind-b profit`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` TRUE
-- E5-17: education and promoting a candidate (put forward as ancillary): does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`, `ind-b candidate`) `ind-b none` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-18: E5-11 for an applicant: does not meet.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b applicant` (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `ind-b intended PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- E5-19: the Commissioner MUST publish and maintain guidance on the charity test: the duty stands, and the Commissioner's act discharges it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` `Art 5(4) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on the charity test`
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 5(4) the Commissioner must publish and maintain guidance on the charity test` 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`publish and maintain guidance` `the Commissioner` `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`) 1))
-- E5-20: any person determining the test must have regard to the guidance.
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `any person` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the court` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- E5-21: in their other functions, the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of one; not others.
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the Charity Tribunal` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a registered charity` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `a governor` FALSE TRUE TRUE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `the court` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` `any person` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- E5-22: consulted representatives, the Minister and others: 5(6)(a) satisfied.
#ASSERT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- E5-23: the Minister not consulted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- E5-24: no representatives consulted though there are some.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- E5-25: consulted, but no report published: 5(6) not complied with.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `ind-b A` (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `ind-b A` (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 4 1))
-- E5-25: the 5(6) duty chain: consulting alone does not discharge it; consulting then publishing does.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 5(6) the Commissioner must consult and publish a report before issuing or amending guidance` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`consult` `the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 1))
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 5(6) the Commissioner must consult and publish a report before issuing or amending guidance` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`consult` `the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 1, EVENT `the Commissioner` (`publish a report on the views on the consultation and the reasons for the decision on the guidance` `the Commissioner`) 2))
-- E5-23 as a trace: a consultation that left out the Minister does not discharge the first duty.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 5(6) the Commissioner must consult and publish a report before issuing or amending guidance` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`consult` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE TRUE) 1, EVENT `the Commissioner` (`publish a report on the views on the consultation and the reasons for the decision on the guidance` `the Commissioner`) 2))
-- E5-27: the 5(7) duty of the Commissioner arises after guidance is issued, and the copy discharges it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (`Art 5(7) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with the guidance and the report` `ind-b A` (YMD 2020 6 1) 30)
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 5(7) the Commissioner must provide the Minister with the guidance and the report` `ind-b A` (YMD 2020 6 1) 30) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`provide to the Minister a copy of the issued or amended guidance and the report` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- E5-28: the 5(8) duty is the Minister's.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (`Art 5(8) the Minister must lay the guidance and the report before the States` `ind-b A` (YMD 2020 7 1) 30)
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 5(8) the Minister must lay the guidance and the report before the States` `ind-b A` (YMD 2020 7 1) 30) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Minister` (`lay a copy of the guidance and report before the States` `the Minister`) 1))
-- E5-29: the 5(3) power is the Minister's.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` `Art 5(3) the Minister may disapply Article 5(2)`
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 5(3) the Minister may disapply Article 5(2)` 0 (LIST EVENT `the Minister` (`make an Order disapplying the bar on control by a Minister, a member of the States Assembly or an equivalent` `the Minister`) 1))
-- E5-10..E5-12 through the limb that decides: the bar.
#ASSERT `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` TRUE) `the Chief Minister` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(2) bars an entity that otherwise meets the charity test`
-- E5-04 through the limb that decides: no charitable purpose.
#ASSERT `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b shop`)) (LIST `ind-b shop`) `ind-b none` `the Chief Minister` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: the entity has no charitable purpose`

§ `Article 5 -- each other reading of the forks of G2 that Article 5 reads`

-- F2.1 B (vacuous truth): an entity with no purposes passes 5(1)(a) (A-01 reading A).
#ASSERT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` EMPTY) EMPTY
-- F2.1 A (taken by the encoder; my A-01 reading B, taken weakly): no purposes, no pass.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` EMPTY) EMPTY
-- F2.1 C (ancillary purposes alone suffice): E5-04's entity passes 5(1)(a) on that reading, as the reading says.
#ASSERT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b shop`)) (LIST `ind-b shop`)
-- F2.1 every reading: E5-03's non-charitable, non-ancillary purpose fails 5(1)(a).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`, `ind-b profit`)) (LIST `ind-b education`, `ind-b profit`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`, `ind-b profit`)) (LIST `ind-b education`, `ind-b profit`)
-- F2.2 B (caught however the person is to act): E5-13's personal-capacity governor is caught on that reading.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.2 read as B` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `a member of the States Assembly` FALSE) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
-- F2.3 A (taken; my A-02 reading A): the Minister for Health (no office of Article 1), acting as Minister, defeats the test.
#ASSERT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `ind-b A` `the Chief Minister` (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` NOTHING) TRUE)
-- F2.3 B (only the Minister of Article 1): the Minister for Health is not caught; the Chief Minister is when the text names the Chief Minister.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B` `the Chief Minister` (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` NOTHING) TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 5(2) the constitution defeats the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.3 read as B` `the Chief Minister` (`ind-b a constitution permitting` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` (`a Minister` (JUST `the Chief Minister`)) TRUE)
-- F2.6 and F2.4 B (promptness counted in days): 30 days from 2020-06-01; day 30 is in time when the day of the event is not counted, not when it is.
#ASSERT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.4 read as B` (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 7 1)) FALSE 30
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.4 read as B` (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 7 2)) FALSE 30
-- F2.7 B (the consultation may fall on the day of issue).
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.7 read as B` (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` `ind-b A` (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 6 1))

§ `Article 6 -- charitable purposes (rows E6-a to E6-5d)`

-- E6-a to E6-o (the heads with no narrowing clause).
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the prevention or relief of poverty`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of education`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of religion`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of health`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the saving of lives`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of citizenship or community development`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of the arts, heritage, culture or science`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of human rights, conflict resolution or reconciliation`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the promotion of religious or racial harmony`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of environmental protection or improvement`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage`
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `the advancement of animal welfare`
-- E6-h: sport involving physical skill and exertion.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "public participation in football" (JUST `the advancement of public participation in sport`)) (`ind-b sport facts` (JUST TRUE))
-- E6-i: recreational facilities open to the public at large (object of improving conditions of life assumed in the head).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "a public recreation ground" (JUST `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`)) (`ind-b recreation facts` NOTHING (JUST TRUE))
-- E6-l: equality and diversity.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "promoting equality and diversity" (JUST `the promotion of equality and diversity`)) `ind-b equality and diversity facts`
-- E6-p1: a purpose analogous to (a)-(o) (the analogy recorded as the head).
#ASSERT `ind-b the head alone is charitable` `any other purpose that may reasonably be regarded as analogous to one of the above`
-- E6-p2: no head, not analogous: not charitable.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "private profit" NOTHING) `ind-b no Article 6 facts`
-- E6-2a: prevention or relief of sickness: within (d) by 6(2)(a).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "relieving sickness" NOTHING) (`ind-b clarification facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- E6-2b1: urban regeneration: within (f).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "urban regeneration" NOTHING) (`ind-b clarification facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- E6-2b2: promotion of volunteering: within (f).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "promoting volunteering" NOTHING) (`ind-b clarification facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- E6-2c1: football (skill and exertion): sport.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "football" (JUST `the advancement of public participation in sport`)) (`ind-b sport facts` (JUST TRUE))
-- E6-2c2 and E6-2c3: chess (no physical exertion) or exertion without skill: not sport, not (h).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "chess" (JUST `the advancement of public participation in sport`)) (`ind-b sport facts` (JUST FALSE))
-- E6-2d1: facilities primarily for the elderly in need: within (i).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "a day centre for the elderly" (JUST `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`)) (`ind-b recreation facts` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE))
-- E6-2d2: facilities available to female members of the public at large: within (i).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "a women's swimming pool" (JUST `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`)) (`ind-b recreation facts` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE))
-- E6-2d3: a members-only club, no one in need: not within (i).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "a private club's facilities" (JUST `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`)) (`ind-b recreation facts` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE))
-- E6-2e: relief of the elderly by accommodation: within (n).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "housing the elderly in need" NOTHING) (`ind-b clarification facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- E6-2f: humanism: within (p) by 6(2)(f), with no head recorded.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (Purpose WITH description IS "advancing humanism", head IS NOTHING, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE) `ind-b no Article 6 facts`
-- E6-3a: the States add a head on the Commissioner's recommendation: within the power.
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- E6-3b: no recommendation: outside.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` FALSE (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- E6-3c: an explanatory 6(2) sub-paragraph for a head so added: within.
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- E6-3d: a 6(2) sub-paragraph narrowing an original head: outside.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- E6-3e: the power is the States': the deontic is the States' permission, and an act of the States exercises it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (`Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (`Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the States` (`make Regulations adding sub-paragraphs to the list of charitable purposes or to its explanations` `the States`) 1))
-- E6-4a: Regulations removing or restricting an original head: outside.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- E6-4b: Regulations altering 6(5): outside.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
-- E6-5a, E6-5b: advancing a political party / promoting a candidate abroad: neither charitable nor ancillary.
#ASSERT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` (`ind-b political purpose` "advancing a political party" NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b political purpose` "promoting a candidate for election abroad" NOTHING FALSE) `ind-b no Article 6 facts`
-- E6-5c: promoting a candidate framed as advancement of citizenship: not charitable.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b political purpose` "promoting a candidate, as citizenship" (JUST `the advancement of citizenship or community development`) FALSE) `ind-b no Article 6 facts`
-- E6-5c: nor ancillary.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(1)(a)(ii) the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose` `ind-b candidate`
-- E6-5d: campaigning on a policy issue is not caught by 6(5).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` (`ind-b purpose` "campaigning on a policy issue" NOTHING)
-- F2.5 B: a philosophical belief counts as advancing religion (6(1)(c)) only on the second reading; F2.5 A (taken): not within (c).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST (`ind-b with no facts` (Purpose WITH description IS "humanism", head IS NOTHING, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE))))
#ASSERT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST (`ind-b with no facts` (Purpose WITH description IS "humanism", head IS NOTHING, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS FALSE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS TRUE))))

§ `Article 7 -- public benefit (rows E7-01 to E7-10)`

-- E7-01: 7(2) and 7(3) bind the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court.
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Commissioner` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the Charity Tribunal` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `the court` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- E7-02: not a governor or anyone else.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `a governor` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(1) Articles 7(2) and 7(3) apply to the person` `any person` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- E7-03: the Commissioner, on an entity benefiting only one natural person: no public benefit, whatever was found; the charity test fails.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (`ind-b determination of an entity benefiting only identified persons, by` `the Commissioner` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b charity test` `ind-b A` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` (`ind-b determination of an entity benefiting only identified persons, by` `the Commissioner` TRUE) FALSE
-- E7-04: the tribunal and the court, on a group of identified natural persons: no public benefit.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (`ind-b determination of an entity benefiting only identified persons, by` `the Charity Tribunal` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (`ind-b determination of an entity benefiting only identified persons, by` `the court` TRUE)
-- E7-03 on every reading of F2.10: the 7(3)(b) outcome does not depend on it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as B` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (`ind-b determination of an entity benefiting only identified persons, by` `the Commissioner` TRUE)
-- E7-05: identified people AND the public at large: the finding decides.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner`
-- E7-06: with no finding of public benefit, no conclusion that the entity provides it (it is not presumed from the purpose).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST (`ind-b with no facts` (`ind-b purpose` "advancement of religion" (JUST `the advancement of religion`))))) `ind-b no PB by the Commissioner`
-- E7-06: a finding reached by presuming the purpose to be for the public benefit gives no answer that it provides it (F2.10 A refuses; C answers no; B lets the finding stand, as that reading says).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) `ind-b determination that presumed public benefit`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as C` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) `ind-b determination that presumed public benefit`
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.10 read as B` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) `ind-b determination that presumed public benefit`
-- E7-07: a section of the public, an unduly restrictive fee considered: a consideration, not an automatic answer; the finding decides either way.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (`ind-b determination of a fee-charging section of the public, finding` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (`ind-b determination of a fee-charging section of the public, finding` FALSE)
-- E7-08: the comparison of private benefit with public benefit is a consideration: the finding decides.
#ASSERT `Art 7(2) the determiner had the regard that Article 7(2) requires` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner`
-- E7-09: the 5(4) guidance must cover public benefit.
#ASSERT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` (LIST `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`, `the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7(4) the guidance published under Article 5(4) gives guidance on public benefit` (LIST `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test`)
-- E7-10: an entity benefiting one legal person is not caught by 7(3)(b): the finding decides.
#ASSERT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) `ind-b PB by the Commissioner`
-- E7-02 as rules: the 7(3) prohibitions bind the Commissioner and not a governor.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (`Art 7(3)(a) the person determining must not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` `the Commissioner` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`)
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (`Art 7(3)(a) the person determining must not presume a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` `a governor` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`)
#ASSERT `ind-b nothing is owed under` (`Art 7(3)(b) the person determining must not treat an entity that benefits only identified natural persons as providing public benefit` `any person` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`)

§ `Reading checks for G2 added at review (F2.6 B, F2.11 B, F2.12 B)`

-- F2.4 B with F2.6 B (days counted, the day of the event the first day): 30 days from 2020-06-01 end on 2020-06-30.
#ASSERT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` (`Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` OF `F2.1 A`, `F2.2 A`, `F2.3 A`, `F2.4 B`, `F2.5 A`, `F2.6 B`, `F2.7 A`, `F2.8 A`, `F2.9 A`, `F2.10 A`, `F2.11 A`, `F2.12 A`, `F2.13 A`, `F2.14 A`) (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 6 30)) FALSE 30
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(7) the Commissioner provided the Minister with the guidance and the report in time` (`Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` OF `F2.1 A`, `F2.2 A`, `F2.3 A`, `F2.4 B`, `F2.5 A`, `F2.6 B`, `F2.7 A`, `F2.8 A`, `F2.9 A`, `F2.10 A`, `F2.11 A`, `F2.12 A`, `F2.13 A`, `F2.14 A`) (YMD 2020 6 1) (JUST (YMD 2020 7 1)) FALSE 30
-- F2.11 B (either equality or diversity suffices): a purpose that promotes diversity but not equality is within (l) on that reading, not on the reading taken.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`ind-b purpose` "promoting diversity" (JUST `the promotion of equality and diversity`)) (`Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE, `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE, `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE, `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING, `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose promotes equality` IS JUST FALSE, `the purpose promotes diversity` IS JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "promoting diversity" (JUST `the promotion of equality and diversity`)) (`Facts about a purpose under Article 6` WITH `the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom they are primarily intended` IS JUST TRUE, `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering` IS FALSE, `the purpose is rural or urban regeneration` IS FALSE, `the purpose is the promotion of civic responsibility, volunteering, the voluntary sector or the effectiveness or efficiency of registered charities` IS FALSE, `the sport involves physical skill and exertion` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage` IS NOTHING, `the facilities or activities are available to members of the public at large or to male or female members of the public at large` IS NOTHING, `the purpose is relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, given by the provision of accommodation or care` IS FALSE, `the purpose promotes equality` IS JUST FALSE, `the purpose promotes diversity` IS JUST TRUE)
-- F2.12 B (5(6) to 5(8) apply to any guidance): guidance on the operation of the Law alone is in scope on that reading, not on the reading taken.
#ASSERT `Art 5(6) Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to the guidance` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.12 read as B` (LIST `the operation of the Law, including the duties of governors and the charity test`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(6) Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to the guidance` `ind-b A` (LIST `the operation of the Law, including the duties of governors and the charity test`)


§ `Moved from ind-b-tests-disagree.l4: rows E6-2d4 and V-20 of expectations.md, which failed or refused before the repair of G2 (R1, R2) and hold now`

-- E6-2d4: recreational facilities open to the public at large WITHOUT the object of improving the conditions of life: not within (i).
-- The only way to say "recreational facilities" to this encoding is the head (i); it has no fact for the object of 6(1)(i).
-- AS AUTHORED (before the integrator's edit, which only names the fixture that states the object false): ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "a public amusement arcade, not for improving conditions of life" (JUST `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`)) (`ind-b recreation facts` NOTHING (JUST TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `ind-b A` (`ind-b purpose` "a public amusement arcade, not for improving conditions of life" (JUST `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`)) (`ind-b recreation facts without the object` NOTHING (JUST TRUE))

-- V-20: a body that is not an "entity" (no kind of Article 2(1); domain.l4: "kinds of entity ... empty if it is not an entity") cannot meet the charity test, whatever its purposes.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` `ind-b A` (Entity WITH name IS "B, an NPO body corporate, on 15 October 2025", `standing on the register` IS `ind-b applicant`, `kinds of entity` IS EMPTY, `is a Jersey entity` IS FALSE, governors IS EMPTY, purposes IS LIST (`ind-b purpose` "the advancement of education" (JUST `the advancement of education`))) (LIST `ind-b education`) `ind-b none` `the Chief Minister` `ind-b PB by the Commissioner` FALSE
